ence sony showed it at their panel  before anybody in the world saw it and  unfortunately  but also kind of fortunately it looks  like that's what we're about to see  they're either going to show an actual  trailer or footage  however unfortunately this is probably  not going to be released to the public  it's going to be up to somebody to leak  it if the public is going to see it  it's already been confirmed that no  types of recording devices  at all are going to be allowed inside of  the session and all phones are going to  have to be turned off  and i actually really wouldn't be  surprised if they made them do more like  put their phones in lockers or something  like  that and again do not expect this  footage to go  public at the same time this isn't going  to be like marvel studios showing  something and then at the same time it  pops up on youtube  unfortunately disney has already  confirmed that sony is the one  handling all of the trailer releases and  the marketing disney is in the loop and  aware of everything that they're going  to do and when they're going to do it  but sony is handling everything it's up  to them and this was confirmed by  disney's president of marketing  however there is some good news to this  because even though people can't show  footage  they can still talk about what they saw  even though they're forcing their  cameras off and turning cell phones off  you can't stop people  hundreds of people from going out and  talking about what they saw  and of course there are probably going  to be some very loyal spider-man fans  out there who probably can't wait to go  to the internet and share what they saw  so despite what happens if any type of  footage  is shown for spider-man no way home we  are going to hear about that footage and  know what it is  on august 23rd i almost hope it actually  is  footage and not the actual trailer and  here's why i've said this at kind of the  end of some of my videos and i know the  majority of people don't watch all the  way till the end so i'll say it now in  the middle  i have personally heard from one of my  sources that the very first teaser  trailer  for spider-man no way home is not going  to contain the other spider-man  i was specifically told that when the  marketing campaigns  do start for spider-man no way home they  aren't going to start marketing the  other two spider-man until about either  halfway or two-thirds into the campaign  that means the teaser trailer is not  going to have them and that means  probably the first trailer that we get  isn't going to have them either  however i am specifically talking about  the other two spider-man so that doesn't  mean that we can't see  alfred molina's doggock show up it  doesn't mean that we won't see jamie  foxx's electro  i definitely think we'll see signs of  the multiverse  spider-verse but they're still going to  try and build up hype and the way you do  that is you start with a teaser  tease a little bit then do a full-on  trailer kind of explaining what the  story is and then  you reveal the other two and i still  debate in my mind on whether or not they  should even show the other two before  the movie comes out  i guess it's irrelevant because the very  first day the movie comes out  everybody's going to be talking about it  and everybody's going to know  so i guess if you're sony you just beat  them to it and show it in the trailer  now in terms of when are we actually  going to see the trailer  the general public when is it going to  go on youtube or on tv  we don't really have an exact time frame  right now but daniel rpk at one point in  time said that we would have to have  another shanxi trailer and another  eternals trailer before getting  spider-man well  we've had that other shang-chi trailer  and the other day he actually tweeted  out stating that he thinks that it will  be  with either shangqi or venom 2. and  venom 2 actually makes a lot of sense  because again that is coming from sony  and it actually  seems like right now sony's marketing  priority  is venom 2 which makes sense because it  is coming out first  and they just released their full  trailer for the movie  last week actually not even it was only  five days ago it was this week which  means the full  trailer released literally less than two  months before the movie is actually  coming out which means they released the  teaser trailer  four months before the actual movie is  coming out so we can assume that they're  going to follow somewhat of a similar  pattern for spider-man no way home  now of course like some rumors have been  going around there is  always the possibility that they could  delay spider-man no way home they could  delay its release date  obviously nobody wants this but with all  the different variants of kobid  and yes i did use variant intentionally  there it seems like studios are kind of  freaking out again that people won't go  to theaters  because venom and spiderman no way home  aren't going to be released anywhere  else but in the theaters  these are theatrical releases only so  there is that possibility  that spider-man no way home could be  delayed especially if you consider the  fact that they're actually doing  reshoots right now for the film  now i hope it's not i really hope it's  not but if they did  show a trailer at cinemacon they could  actually reveal  a new release date so keep that in mind  and be prepared for that because that  could happen  but again keep in mind overall good news  because whatever they show  at cinemacon we are going to hear about  we are going to get a  full description of so even though i am  100 convinced that the public is not  going to see whatever footage or trailer  for spider-man no way home that is going  to be shown at cinemacon  i am convinced that we will be getting  an exact description of what they saw  because this happened with spider-man  far from home  sony showed the trailer the actual  trailer before the public saw it and  then everybody knew what it was  we didn't see it but we had a very  accurate description  and side note marvel is also going to be  there and they've actually done this  before too before we got any footage for  the eternals they showed it at ccxp  and apparently they're actually going to  be showing a full screening of  shanghi somewhere at cinemacon so marvel  is going to be there and have a presence  as well which  is good news because that means the  likelihood of sony showing spider-man no  way home footage is very  very high and who knows if marvel  studios does do their own panel we could  get a description for shang qi  the eternals miss marvel hawkeye moon  knight  all of their upcoming stuff we could  learn a great deal more about  but of course i know that everybody at  this point is pretty much just concerned  about that spider-man no way home  trailer which i completely  understand hopefully this means that the  actual trailer will come out not too  long after the footage is shown at  cinemacon  but keep an eye out the 23rd for more  information about whatever they show  at cinemacon because we are going to  find out then so  be sure to subscribe and hit the  notification bell so you don't miss out  on any of the videos and you can follow  me on twitter and  instagram because i always do live  updates on there let me know your  thoughts on the video  in the comment down below don't forget  to like the video and as always thank  you all so much for watching  woof

